/S /H1
/T (Executive Summary)
/E (Executive Summary)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Millions of Americans in rural and underserved areas face unequal access to primary healthcare, leading to higher rates of preventable disease, increased reliance on emergency services, and poorer health outcomes. Despite a recent overall increase in the health workforce, severe shortages of primary care physicians persist in health professional shortage areas. Here, Root Cause Analysis \(RCA\) identifies workforce maldistribution as a primary driver of this issue, with further analysis pointing to deprioritization of primary care investment through structural health financing and policy neglect as a fundamental root cause.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This policy brief explores these challenges through a national lens, drawing evidence from Appalachia, the Mississippi Delta, Native American reservations, and the rural Midwest - rural regions that adequately exemplify the consequences of workforce maldistribution. Potential solutions could include reforming health financing, strengthening the health workforce, tackling barriers faced by non-physician providers, and improving access to telehealth services through policy.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
