137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Economic barriers are another contributor to reinforced provider shortages. Lower inpatient reimbursement rates in rural areas disincentivize PC practice, with rural hospitals receiving 90.6% that of Traditional Medicare rates compared to their urban counterparts \(18\). Furthermore, the closures of 150+ rural hospitals since 2010 have significantly attenuated PC access and practice opportunities \(22\). Meanwhile, low private insurance market competition has led to higher uninsured rates in rural communities \(12.6%\) compared to more urban ones \(10.9%\), discouraging timely care utilization \(23\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
