142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (3.4 - Structural & Policy Failures)
/E (3.4 - Structural & Policy Failures)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Beyond workforce and infrastructure challenges, systemic policy failures contribute to fragmented and inefficient service delivery. The US healthcare system prioritizes specialist-driven care, offering higher reimbursement rates for procedures over PC services \(27,37\). In addition, state-level restrictions on nurse practitioners \(NPs\) and physician assistants \(PAs\) limit their ability to provide independent PC, despite evidence that they improve access \(38\). Interstate licencing barriers further restrict provider mobility, exacerbating regional disparities. Meanwhile, community health workers \(CHWs\), who play a fundamental role in CDM and preventative care, remain underfunded despite their proven effectiveness \(29\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
